      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE PROCESS FOR REVIEWING THE FORM 990 BEGINS WITH AN INTERNAL REVIEW CONDUCTED BY THE CONTROLLER, WHO ENSURES THAT ALL FINANCIAL DATA IS ACCURATE AND COMPLETE. AFTER THE CONTROLLER'S REVIEW, THE FORM 990 IS THEN PASSED TO THE TREASURER OF THE BOARD FOR REVIEW. ONCE THE TREASURER HAS REVIEWED AND APPROVED THE FORM, IT IS DISCUSSED WITH THE CEO, WHO GIVES FINAL APPROVAL. AFTER SUBMISSION, THE FORM 990 IS DISTRIBUTED TO THE FINANCE COMMITTEE FOR THEIR REVIEW.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>COMPLIANCE TRAINING FOR THE BOARD IS DONE ANNUALLY AT THE FEBRUARY OR MARCH BOARD MEETING. DURING THIS TRAINING, "INTERESTED PERSONS" ARE REVIEWED AND EACH BOARD MEMBER IS THEN REQUIRED TO FILL OUT AND SIGN AN "INTERESTED PERSONS" STATEMENT.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A SUBCOMMITTEE OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS REVIEWS COMPENSATION AND RECOMMENDS CHANGES IF NECESSARY. THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS MUST APPROVE COMPENSATION OF KEY EMPLOYEESS EACH YEAR. MINUTES OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS' MEETINGS RECORD COMPENSATION DELIBERATIONS AND APPROVAL.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>DOCUMENTS ARE AVAILABLE UPON WRITTEN REQUEST TO THE CONTROLLER OR CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
